  "metadata": {
    "title": "Production line dataset for task scheduling and energy optimization - Schedule Optimization",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.4106746",
    "publication_date": "2020-11-05",
    "description": "<p>The case study of this dataset uses real production data, provided by a textile company that manufactures hang tags. Their working schedule is from 7h00 of Monday to 23h00 of Saturday. This dataset uses a period of 5 minutes for all task durations and energy data. The case study considers a six-day period from 7h00 of Monday to 23h00 of Saturday. The scheduling algorithm was used for three machines that share the same cell.<br>\n<br>\nThe API can be found at &lt;http://www.gecad.isep.ipp.pt/api/spear/&gt;<br>\n<br>\nFile Description:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li>Input_JSON_Schedule_Optimization - JSON input data for the schedule optimization</li>\n\t<li>Output_JSON_Schedule_Optimization -&nbsp;JSON output data for the schedule optimization</li>\n\t<li>Output_Statistics_Schedule_Optimization - Excel output schedule optimization statistics</li>\n</ul>",
